#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61404ce4-ecb2-5ab7-bff5-3dc72be79709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61404ce4-ecb2-5ab7-bff5-3dc72be79709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363044} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac414bdb-1e9c-501d-94fc-5ad66fcd3a37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3844a42-8aa0-5eb9-a1d0-267d67a2e8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-348756" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069699/assets/77004c9040818fbc254b9564b9c5821536ef65fcc77f6765b56d2e8524c24ed4.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1 & =4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2({sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))+1 \\\\  & =4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(2(cos\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(2cos\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(3sin\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+5x)\\,|}_{-3\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+5\\cdot 0)-(3sin\\,(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))+5(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =(0+0)-(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\frac{15\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(0)-(0-\\frac{15\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70727f01-13ef-5922-aecb-158776ec5560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70727f01-13ef-5922-aecb-158776ec5560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363047} :answer-field/id #uuid "09c11847-188c-5fd0-96e8-0d9bd3c0d3da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "889fb234-aee7-55cc-940a-a33b6448e53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348844" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }6{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }6{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{[x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi } \\\\  & =3[6\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{3})-(3\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{3}))] \\\\  & =3[6\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(3\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))] \\\\  & =3(6\\pi -3\\pi ) \\\\  & =9\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297647da-3ab3-5dcc-9a0f-48a9dc1e495f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327583} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3104d2-922a-56ba-ad75-57e2cb7a3a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327584} {:answer/id #uuid "d2af47ef-76c7-5f0b-8538-94f85021dbeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327585} {:answer/id #uuid "d65d5927-bfb8-5799-9a36-4be823721147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327586} {:answer/id #uuid "5984ac9f-2835-5f33-a158-60355d52e40e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "297647da-3ab3-5dcc-9a0f-48a9dc1e495f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327583} :answer-field/id #uuid "20bf7902-d8bf-522c-b9ef-2ee403332062" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d3c3918e-b0d8-54bc-84f9-50f26c7e5758" :question/math-academy-id "q-51126" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}({cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x={cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}({cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /24} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88eef018-64bb-5b92-9c2f-1ec72b23190b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361738} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9fa166-eeae-5071-b0a1-4bd3d34b9996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361739} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e0e150-4f95-50ed-81b8-24f3f0d94910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361740} {:answer/id #uuid "3c91618c-4258-5a14-8cd8-01e1586709c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361741} {:answer/id #uuid "46b5ef69-26de-5cc2-a63e-ea09ebba0936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5e0e150-4f95-50ed-81b8-24f3f0d94910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361740} :answer-field/id #uuid "16d79c9f-2069-5cd9-b62f-5a63f18b029f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff8c9059-4ccd-5c34-b361-0250f8da7c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-74408" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [5-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int [5-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-4(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d0b2b8-6037-5e30-8c7e-dc875e31d807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd8c527-f2cf-5bcd-b204-b5e9811dfd6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288728} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc46874-f687-57e2-aaba-12c246abf376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288729} {:answer/id #uuid "67419508-3f81-53e7-9110-63ca99506a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288730} {:answer/id #uuid "848fb85e-72a1-5896-93c7-89c1071885f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d0b2b8-6037-5e30-8c7e-dc875e31d807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288727} :answer-field/id #uuid "65c462af-9369-5e19-acfc-b87c6a056b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b373498-84db-5708-b542-71c40a8177eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-74410" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
